{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "An Emotional Week"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Enough Is Enough"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 4}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Relate information about common solutions to problems."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le04ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "What Clauses and Long Noun Phrases as Subjects"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You shift emphasis from the beginning to another part of the sentence by using <span class=\"italic\">what</span>, <span class=\"italic\">that</span> and <span class=\"italic\">who</span> phrases as subjects."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Usually, you focus on the person doing the action in this case, the comedian telling jokes. <br/>   Example: <span class=\"italic\">John told a funny joke.</span><br/><br/> If we wish to place emphasis on another part of the sentence, we isolate that part and package up the rest of the information into a <span class=\"italic\">what</span>-phrase (or sometimes a <span class=\"italic\">that</span>-clause.)<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">What John said was funny."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">That</span> with a subordinated content clause can function as the subject of a sentence.<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">That he imitated our teacher was funny.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">What</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Who</span> serves as a placeholder for the content of the noun phrase that has been moved to the end of the sentence. The effect is that more emphasis is placed on the initial content.<br/> Example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">What was hilarious was his imitation of the teacher.</span><br/>        <span class=\"italic\"> Who he should have made fun of was the principal."}, {"type": "example", "content": "That I haven't completely lost it is a miracle!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What she needs is to increase her emotional intelligence."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What she thought is that I was criticizing her."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What she said was that I was wasting her time."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Who I have to feel good about helping is myself! "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Tag Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use tag questions to ask for clarification and confirmation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Question tags are short questions at the end of statements.<br/> They are mainly used in speech when we want to:<br/> <ul><li><span class=\"strong\">confirm that something is true or not</span>, or</li> <li><span class=\"strong\">to encourage a reply</span> from the person we are speaking to.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "A <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018yes'.<br/> <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">were</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> you?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">are</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> you?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">has</span> a brother, <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> she?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">can</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> he?</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "A negative statement is followed by a positive question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018no'.<br/> <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">were</span> you? </li> <li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">are</span> you?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> have a brother, <span class=\"strong\">does</span> she?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can</span> he?</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If the main verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">modal</span> verb, the tag will be the same.<br/> For all other main verbs, use the tag <span class=\"italic\">do/does</span> or <span class=\"italic\">did/didn't</span>.<br/><br/> Look at the examples in the chart:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He is/was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"isn't/was't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"aren't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"couldn't we?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"won't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She has/had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't/didn't she?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He likes \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You like\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You liked \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"didn't you?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You haven't told off someone else on the bus, have you?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You didn't tell her that, did you?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm not deranged, am I?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "She didn't want to listen, did she? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's her loss, isn't it?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to tell someone off"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to reprimand or scold someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You haven't told off someone else on the bus, have you?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob10aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about reactions and behavior in different situations."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to be all ears"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to be very eager to hear what someone is going to say"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm all ears."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob10aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "deranged"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "unable to think or act in a normal or logical way "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm not deranged, am I?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob10aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to lose it"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to become very angry or emotionally upset"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That I haven't completely lost it is a miracle!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob10aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to achieve"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to reach something by working hard"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When people have emotional intelligence, they function better and achieve more in the work environment."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob10aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "resistant "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "opposed to something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She was really resistant to hearing what I had to say."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob10aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "insignificant"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "small or unimportant"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She made me feel really insignificant."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob10aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "receptive"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "willing to listen or accept ideas"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She doesn't seem like she's very receptive to change."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob10aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "On the internet, watch a movie or TV show with a lot of dialogue between two people."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose a dialogue section that is about 20 seconds long."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Listen to the section as many times as you need."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down the dialogue using reported speech."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice reading the dialogue aloud."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write about reactions and behavior."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I shift emphasis by using <span class=\"italic\">what</span>, <span class=\"italic\">who</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">that</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask for clarification and confirmation. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I transcribe a dialogue in reported speech."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can write about  reactions and behavior."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can shift emphasis by using <span class=\"italic\">what</span>, <span class=\"italic\">who</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">that</span>. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can ask for clarification and confirmation. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What is the best way to deal with criticism from your boss?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What is constructive criticism and how can it be beneficial?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Criticism is hard to take."}]}, {"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "id": 1}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}]}], "type": "STI", "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "co